.TH GARB 1 "November 2026" "Grintion-OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
garb \- Grintion Archive and Package Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B garb
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B garb
is the native package management utility for Grintion-OS. It provides atomic transactions, rollback generations, binary package delta archives, mirror ranking, and cryptographically verified package installations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fIPKG\fR
Install one or more packages.
.TP
\fBremove\fR \fIPKG\fR
Remove installed packages.
.TP
\fBupgrade\fR
Upgrade all packages, creating a new atomic rollback generation.
.TP
\fBgenerations\fR
List recorded package generation snapshots.
.TP
\fBrollback-generation\fR \fIID\fR
Roll back package files and database state to a previous generation.
.TP
\fBhold\fR \fIPKG\fR / \fBunhold\fR \fIPKG\fR
Prevent or permit package upgrades.
.TP
\fBdelta-create\fR \fI--old OLD --new NEW --out DELTA\fR
Generate a delta archive between two canonical .garb packages. The new archive
must have been built by the current \fBgarb build\fR format.
.TP
\fBdelta-apply\fR \fI--old OLD --delta DELTA --out NEW --index INDEX --key PUBKEY\fR
Reconstruct a package from a delta and verify the result's SHA-256 against the
signed repository index before writing the output.
.TP
\fBmirror-rank\fR
Benchmark and sort repository mirrors by network response speed.
.SH AUTHORS
Grintion-OS Core Team.

